  "construction": "Random Clifford encoder (16-20 layers of random two-qubit Clifford gates on random qubit pairs) gives a parent [[60,16]] code; all of its logical operators of weight below 11 are enumerated and 3 logical operators are added as stabilizers (expurgation), chosen by solving over GF(2) so that each low-weight logical anticommutes with one of them. The generators listed here are a low-weight generating set of the same stabilizer group, found by an information-set search, to meet the weight-32 cap.",
  "origin": "submission",
  "novelty": "unknown",
  "date": "2026-11-08",
  "references": [
   "https://github.com/MarinAndreGirard/qubit-stabilizer-codes-2026"
  ],
  "notes": "Code round2-002 of the release https://github.com/MarinAndreGirard/qubit-stabilizer-codes-2026 (codes/stabilizers/n060_k013_d11.txt). d >= 11 was proved by an exhaustive meet-in-the-middle search over all Paulis of weight <= 5 with a visit count equal to the closed form; see verify/ in the release. At its (n, k) the codetables.de lower bound on 4 November 2026 was below 11. The board entry 60-13-11 has the same parameters but is a different construction (palindromic quasi-cyclic, max check weight 28); this entry is not expected to be equivalent to it."
 },
